ized pointer: undefined behavior","Segmentation fault is the best outcome: virtual memory reports no access; AddressSanitizer catches silent errors too"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["int *p;","{","    int x = 5;","    p = &x;","}   // x died","*p;        // dangling"],"hl":[4,5],"bad":[5],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":17.0,"w":280.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"m0","x":40.0,"y":60.0,"w":56.0,"h":26.0,"text":"1","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m1","x":98.0,"y":60.0,"w":56.0,"h":26.0,"text":"2","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m2","x":156.0,"y":60.0,"w":56.0,"h":26.0,"text":"3","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m3","x":214.0,"y":60.0,"w":56.0,"h":26.0,"text":"4","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":292.0,"y":60.0,"w":56.0,"h":26.0,"text":"?","tone":"red","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":108.0,"lines":["a[4]   // reads someone else's"],"hl":[0],"bad":[0],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":16.0,"w":280.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":330.0,"h":68.0,"text":"==1==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow\nWRITE of size 4 at 0x602000000014\n    #0 main main.c:7","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[10.6,32.6]}]},{"title":"memcpy and friends","sub":"Memory blocks","short":"mem*","main":"Size is in bytes; memmove allows overlap.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["memcpy and memmove","memset and memcmp","Size in bytes"],"captions":["memcpy copies bytes and needs non-overlapping areas; memmove allows overlap and picks the copy direction","memset fills memory with one byte, memcmp compares blocks and returns the sign of the first difference","Size is always in bytes: a common bug is passing the element count instead of n * sizeof(T)"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"m0","x":40.0,"y":50.0,"w":56.0,"h":26.0,"text":"1","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m1","x":98.0,"y":50.0,"w":56.0,"h":26.0,"text":"2","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m2","x":156.0,"y":50.0,"w":56.0,"h":26.0,"text":"3","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m3","x":214.0,"y":50.0,"w":56.0,"h":26.0,"text":"4","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m4","x":272.0,"y":50.0,"w":56.0,"h":26.0,"text":"5","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":90.0,"lines":["memmove(a + 1, a, 4 * sizeof a[0]);"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":9.5,"lh":16.0,"w":320.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":130.0,"text":"result: 1 1 2 3 4 — copied right to left","size":9.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["memset(buf, 0, sizeof buf);","memcmp(a, b, n) < 0   // a < b"],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":320.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"memset(p, 1, 4) on int gives 0x01010101","size":9.5,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["int a[10], b[10];","memcpy(b, a, 10);                 // 10 bytes!","memcpy(b, a, 10 * sizeof a[0]);   // correct"],"hl":[1,2],"bad":[1],"lang":"c","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[16.6,32.6]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"What next","short":"Summary","main":"Next: strings, structs, union.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Addresses","Rules","What next"],"captions":["A pointer holds an address, & takes it, * dereferences; an array is back-to-back elements; a[i] ≡ *(a + i)","An array parameter is a pointer, pass the length; const protects data; nobody checks bounds","Next: strings, structs and union: how data is laid out in memory"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":40.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"&x → address","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":70.0,"y":76.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"*p → value","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":70.0,"y":112.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"a[i] ≡ *(a + i)","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id"